h=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/></svg></div>\n<div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px;margin-top:16px\">\n<div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px\"><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:800\">Two pianos in one</div><div style=\"font-size:16.5px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;margin-top:4px;line-height:1.4\">The keyboard splits into two halves that play in the same octave range.</div></div>\n<div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px\"><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:800\">Side by side</div><div style=\"font-size:16.5px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;margin-top:4px;line-height:1.4\">A teacher or parent plays the same passage next to the learner.</div></div>\n<div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px\"><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:800\">Great for duets</div><div style=\"font-size:16.5px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;margin-top:4px;line-height:1.4\">Siblings can practise the same piece together.</div></div></div><div class=\"foot\"><span>Illustration; the exact split point is set by the FP-10</span><b>PIANOERS.COM</b></div></body></html>"], "roland-fp-10-who-should-buy": [660, "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Schibsted+Grotesk:wght@500;700;800&family=Lora:ital,wght@0,500;1,500&family=Noto+Music&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n<style>*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0}\nbody{width:1200px;height:660px;font-family:\"Schibsted Grotesk\",Arial,sans-serif;background:#f3f6f7;color:#15191c;padding:52px 60px 0;position:relative;overflow:hidden}\n.eyebrow{font-size:20px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2e6475}\nh1{font-size:48px;line-height:1.05;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:8px 0 26px}\n.foot{position:absolute;left:60px;right:60px;bottom:20px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:17px;color:#56666e;font-weight:500}\n.foot b{letter-spacing:.12em;color:#2e6475}\n.card{background:#fff;border:1px solid #d9e2e5;border-radius:20px;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgb(21 25 28/6%),0 8px 24px rgb(21 25 28/6%)}\nsvg text{font-family:\"Schibsted Grotesk\",Arial,sans-serif}\n.mus{font-family:\"Noto Music\",serif}\n</style></head><body><div class=\"eyebrow\">Is it for you?</div><h1>Who should buy the Roland FP-10?</h1><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px\"><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:20px 22px;background:#f2faf5\"><div style=\"font-size:26px;font-weight:800;color:#1f7a4d;margin-bottom:6px\">Buy the FP-10 if\u2026</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#1f7a4d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2713</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You want the best key feel you can get for about $500</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#1f7a4d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2713</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You practise mostly with headphones</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#1f7a4d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2713</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You learn with apps on a phone or tablet (Bluetooth MIDI)</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#1f7a4d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2713</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You want something light enough to move or store</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#1f7a4d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2713</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You may move to an acoustic piano later</span></div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:20px 22px;background:#fdf3f0\"><div style=\"font-size:26px;font-weight:800;color:#b0442d;margin-bottom:6px\">Skip it if\u2026</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You want to stream music through the piano (no Bluetooth audio)</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You need a big, room-filling sound from the speakers</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You want lots of sounds and rhythms built in</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You want three pedals on a matching stand</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You prefer lighter, quieter keys (look at the Yamaha P-145)</span></div></div></div><div class=\"foot\"><span>Pianoers.com \u00b7 Roland FP-10 review</span><b>PIANOERS.COM</b></div></body></html>"], "roland-fp-10-accessories": [600, "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Schibsted+Grotesk:wght@500;700;800&family=Lora:ital,wght@0,500;1,500&family=Noto+Music&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n<style>*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0}\nbody{width:1200px;height:600px;font-family:\"Schibsted Grotesk\",Arial,sans-serif;background:#f3f6f7;color:#15191c;padding:52px 60px 0;position:relative;overflow:hidden}\n.eyebrow{font-size:20px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2e6475}\nh1{font-size:48px;line-height:1.05;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:8px 0 26px}\n.foot{position:absolute;left:60px;right:60px;bottom:20px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:17px;color:#56666e;font-weight:500}\n.foot b{letter-spacing:.12em;color:#2e6475}\n.card{background:#fff;border:1px solid #d9e2e5;border-radius:20px;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgb(21 25 28/6%),0 8px 24px rgb(21 25 28/6%)}\nsvg text{font-family:\"Schibsted Grotesk\",Arial,sans-serif}\n.mus{font-family:\"Noto Music\",serif}\n</style></head><body><div class=\"eyebrow\">Complete the setup</div><h1>What to buy with the Roland FP-10</h1><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px\"><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#2e6475\">SUSTAIN PEDAL</span><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px;background:#fff3d1;color:#8a5a00\">Upgrade first</span></div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800\">Roland DP-10</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;line-height:1.4\">The included pedal switch is on/off only. The DP-10 looks like a real piano pedal and allows half-pedalling.</div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#2e6475\">STAND</span><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px;background:#fff3d1;color:#8a5a00\">Needed</span></div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800\">KSCFP10 or KS-13</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;line-height:1.4\">The dedicated KSCFP10 gives a furniture look; the KS-13 is a simple keyboard stand.</div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#2e6475\">HEADPHONES</span><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px;background:#e2eef1;color:#2e6475\">Useful</span></div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800\">Any closed-back pair</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;line-height:1.4\">The FP-10 has a 3.5 mm mini jack. Studio headphones with a 6.3 mm plug need an adapter.</div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#2e6475\">BENCH</span><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px;background:#fff3d1;color:#8a5a00\">Needed</span></div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800\">Adjustable piano bench</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;line-height:1.4\">Height matters more than looks: forearms level with the keys.</div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#2e6475\">CARRYING BAG</span><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px;background:#e2eef1;color:#2e6475\">Optional</span></div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800\">Roland CB-88RL</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;line-height:1.4\">Only if you will carry the piano around.</div></div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:16px;padding:14px 20px;font-size:17px\">Accessory names from Roland's FP-10 options list. Weight on the KSCFP10 stand with music rest: 20.0 kg (44 lb 2 oz).</div><div class=\"foot\"><span>Pianoers.com \u00b7 Roland FP-10 review</span><b>PIANOERS.COM</b></div></body></html>"], "roland-fp-10-review-featured": [675, "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Schibsted+Grotesk:wght@500;700;800&family=Lora:wght@500&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n<style>*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0}body{width:1200px;height:675px;overflow:hidden;font-family:\"Schibsted Grotesk\",Arial,sans-serif;background:#15191c;color:#fff;position:relative}\n.ph{position:absolute;right:-60px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);width:640px;border-radius:24px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 30px 60px rgb(0 0 0/45%)}.ph img{width:100%;display:block}\n.t{position:absolute;left:64px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);width:530px}.e{font-size:20px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:#f6b31e;font-weight:700}\nh1{font-size:74px;line-height: